      "show_title_separator": true,
      "text": "[#](53341a)This family contains **3 distinct workings**. Each one has its own exact offerings, circles, power, and conditions; use the card belonging to the result you intend.[#]()",
      "title": "Rites of Protection",
      "use_markdown_in_title": false
    },
    {
      "type": "modonomicon:text",
      "anchor": "",
      "condition": {
        "type": "modonomicon:none"
      },
      "show_title_separator": true,
      "text": "[#](53341a)Protection upkeep is continuous: the altar is charged every tick. The barrier itself redraws on the source 20-tick boundary, so its blocks remain renewed without rebuilding the whole wall every tick.[#]()",
      "title": "How It Unfolds",
      "use_markdown_in_title": false
    },
    {
      "type": "modonomicon:text",
      "anchor": "",
      "condition": {
        "type": "modonomicon:none"
      },
      "show_title_separator": false,
      "text": "[#](53341a)Re-click the active circle to end the working and recover its refundable offerings.[#]()",
      "title": " ",
      "use_markdown_in_title": false
    },
    {
      "type": "modonomicon:text",
